  "name": "Warrior",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>As long as wars are raged on distant lands, there will be men and women who fight those wars. The warrior is no mere sword-swinger; he is a skilled combatant, combining strength of arm, knowledge of weaponry, and practiced maneuvers to slice or bludgeon his foes into little red bits. Devoted to the perfection of a single group of weapons, the warrior's meditations upon his favored weapon border on the obsessive, but none can deny his consummate skill.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The warrior stands as the unwavering bulwark and primary damage dealer of any adventuring party, specializing in direct, sustained combat. Their core role involves engaging enemies head-on, leveraging their unparalleled mastery of a wide array of weaponry—from swords and axes to lances and fists—to deliver consistent and impactful strikes.</p><p>Beyond merely dishing out punishment, warriors are adept at shrugging off blows, drawing enemy aggression to protect more vulnerable allies, and maintaining battlefield control through a combination of robust defenses and disciplined tactics. They are the reliable frontline, capable of adapting to diverse threats and utilizing powerful, often flashy, combat arts to turn the tide of battle, ensuring the party's survival and ultimate victory against formidable foes.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The warrior's class skills are Acrobatics (Dex), Climb (Str), Craft (Int), Handle Animal (Cha), Intimidate (Cha), Knowledge (dungeoneering) (Int), Profession (Wis), Ride (Dex), Survival (Wis), and Swim (Str).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>A warrior is proficient with all simple and martial weapons, as well as light, medium, and heavy armor and shields (except tower shields).</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The warrior mainly focuses on Strength for martial combat and Constitution for durability.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
